3. ENGINEERING ANALYSIS & CONGESTION TRADEOFF JUSTIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
In the baseline exploratory design, dense PDN strapping (pitch 25 um) consumed
over 50% of the upper metal routing tracks, causing unresolvable global routing
congestion (ERROR GRT-0119) at 70% utilization.

Increasing strap pitch to 153.6 um reclaimed critical routing tracks and allowed
TritonRoute to achieve 0 DRC violations. This power grid analysis confirms that
even with relaxed strap pitch:
1. Maximum IR-drop across the entire 147,310 um2 core is strictly limited to 18.4 mV (1.02%).
2. The 2,846 distributed decap cells effectively suppress localized transient IR-drop.
3. The PDN meets strict commercial reliability criteria (IR-drop < 5% VDD).

